## Phase 3: Implement command outcomes, deadlines, definitions, and registry

Outcome: immutable command definitions can be validated and registered, and
all lifecycle outcomes and finite timing calculations have one implementation.

- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/driver/command/outcomes.lua`.
  - [x] Implement explicit `ready`, `pending`, `fatal`, and intrinsic-only
        `effect_absent` outcomes.
  - [x] Implement `executed`, explicit `retry`, and structured `failed`
        execution outcomes.
  - [x] Keep public results, private verification receipts, effect receipts,
        attempt receipts, and bounded evidence distinct.
  - [x] Make omitted `effect_receipt` explicitly mean no cleanup-requiring
        effect for every execution outcome.
  - [x] Reject implicit retry inference from `false`, `nil`, thrown errors,
        timeout, or cancellation.
- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/driver/command/deadline.lua`.
  - [x] Use an injected monotonic clock.
  - [x] Calculate one absolute deadline after successful synchronous
        normalization.
  - [x] Centralize remaining-time calculation and one documented rounding
        direction.
  - [x] Preserve evidence and report execution timeout when bounded synchronous
        execution returns after its deadline.
- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/driver/command/definition.lua`.
  - [x] Validate names, kinds, normalize/preflight callbacks, execution policy,
        intrinsic policy, timeouts, diagnostics, claims, and cleanup shape.
  - [x] Enforce the proposal's required callable `preflight` field on every
        command definition and workflow step; only fields marked optional in
        the authoritative definition shapes may be omitted.
  - [x] Require `execute` for every non-workflow definition and require one
        `workflow` while forbidding `execute` for `WORKFLOW`.
  - [x] Require `operation_key` only for `EXPLICIT_RETRY_SAFE`.
  - [x] Require `verify` for `CALLBACK`, forbid it for
        `PRIMARY_OBSERVATION`, and omit it for `EXECUTION_RECEIPT`.
  - [x] Require immutable cleanup policy, callable restore, required cleanup
        verification, supported lifetime, and optional resource projection for
        any definition that can report an effect.
  - [x] Reject effect-producing shapes without cleanup policy and cleanup
        policies for definitions that cannot produce effects.
  - [x] Copy or freeze accepted definitions.
- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/driver/command/registry.lua`.
  - [x] Merge built-in and project definitions deterministically.
  - [x] Reject duplicate names and replacement of reserved built-in names.
  - [x] Preserve source-path and command-name diagnostics for invalid project
        definitions.
- [x] Add structural unit tests separately from behavioral conformance tests.
  - [x] Prove all valid kind/intrinsic/retry combinations.
  - [x] Prove invalid workflow, cleanup, verify, retry, timeout, and reserved
        name combinations fail early.
  - [x] Prove definitions cannot be mutated after registration.
- [x] Reserve behavioral qualification for conformance fixtures.
  - [x] Reserve proof that every normalizer and claims projector is bounded,
        synchronous, and non-yielding.
  - [x] Reserve proof that preflight, claims, and verification callbacks remain
        read-only.
  - [x] Reserve the requirement for each `EXECUTION_RECEIPT` definition to
