### Phase 10A: Consolidate immutable table primitives

Outcome: behavior-preserving immutable table construction is centralized in one
small support module without conflating shallow views, recursive snapshots,
enums, or class-like capability objects.

- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/support/immutable.lua` with two documented operations.
  - [x] Implement `read_only(source, label)` as a shallow proxy over framework-
        owned or already-detached data, preserving indexed reads, `pairs`, array
        length, hidden metatable behavior, and a deterministic label-derived
        mutation error.
  - [x] Implement `freeze(value, label, preserve?)` as a recursive defensive
        snapshot that copies keys and values, rejects cycles, preserves scalar
        values, produces immutable proxies at every table level, and optionally
        retains explicitly recognized framework-owned tokens by identity.
  - [x] Keep the API narrow: do not add copying modes, mutable escape hatches,
        class construction, weak-map ownership, enum validation, serialization,
        or domain-specific policy to the shared module.
- [x] Add `tests/unit/support/immutable_spec.lua` covering shallow aliasing,
      recursive detachment, nested and key mutation rejection, `pairs`, length,
      hidden metatables, deterministic labels, cycles, and the preservation hook.
- [x] Migrate exact shallow-proxy duplication first.
  - [x] Replace `driver/command/outcomes.lua`'s private `read_only` helper while
        preserving outcome provenance weak maps and public-result identity.
  - [x] Replace `driver/command/diagnostics.lua`'s private `read_only` helper
        only after bounded plain-data copying; do not make `read_only` itself a
