## Phase 11: Implement explicit retry-safe execution

Outcome: the uncommon mutation-retry policy is fully available and proven even
though initial built-ins remain `ONCE`.

- [x] Validate documented stable operation key, idempotency guarantee,
      attempt-receipt policy, effect-receipt policy, and a command-specific
      conformance fixture for every `EXPLICIT_RETRY_SAFE` definition.
- [x] Accept another attempt only after an explicit `command.retry` result.
- [x] Retain bounded immutable attempt receipts and correlate every attempt in
      events and diagnostics.
- [x] Register every reported retry-attempt effect immediately with forced
      command lifetime.
- [x] Execute and verify every transaction created since the attempt checkpoint
      before another attempt.
- [x] Terminate retry when prior-attempt cleanup is failed or unconfirmed.
- [x] Re-run preflight, volatile target validation, and claim projection/
      validation before each later attempt.
- [x] Reuse the frozen operation key and original absolute command deadline for
      all attempts.
- [x] Let cleanup use its independent deadline while counting elapsed cleanup
      wall time against the parent command deadline.
- [x] Add a synthetic retry-safe definition that proves eventual success,
      fatality, cancellation, timeout, yielding, no-effect retry, effect cleanup,
      cleanup failure, and no retry inferred from false/nil/throw.
- [x] Add operation-key conformance proving stable bounded scalar derivation
      from the same normalized request.
- [x] Perform a follow-up retry-policy review and confirm no initial built-in
      mutator opts in without its own proof fixture.

Completion criteria:

- [x] A later attempt can never execute on top of an unverified prior-attempt
      effect.
- [x] The runner implements both retry policies from the first production
      release of the new architecture.

## Phase 12: Implement workflows and nested read-only commands

Outcome: composite commands and verification queries share parent ownership,
deadline, cancellation, and trace ancestry without creating parallel public
results.

- [x] Add `src/dwarfspec/driver/command/workflow.lua`.
- [x] Validate workflow definitions.
  - [x] Require unique named steps and one bounded synchronous result projector.
  - [x] Allow `QUERY`, `ASSERTION`, `ACTION`, `STATE_SETTER`, and `FIXTURE`
        steps; reject nested `WORKFLOW` steps.
