## Phase 15A: Encapsulate representative runtime capabilities

Outcome: representative commands consume explicit module-owned framework
capabilities instead of ad hoc bundles of loose functions, while `ds.lua`
remains a composition root and command modules retain lifecycle policy.

- [x] Classify every representative dependency as either a stateless framework
      helper or a stateful run-scoped capability.
  - [x] Let command modules import stateless, dependency-free helpers directly
        only when they have no run identity, mutable state, host ownership, or
        lifecycle responsibility.
  - [x] Record the classification for interaction-target resolution, input
        dispatch, render observation, map-view access, save-game host access,
        text search, and overlay transactions before changing construction.
- [x] Encapsulate each stateful representative capability in a documented
      class-like service module with a narrow public method contract.
  - [x] Move interaction-target resolution out of `ds.lua` into a mount-owned
        resolver service instantiated with the current run's mount context.
  - [x] Represent input dispatch and render observation as cohesive runtime
        services rather than unrelated injected functions.
  - [x] Represent map-view reads, writes, and origin conversion as one
        map-view service used by the reversible state-setter definition.
  - [x] Represent save-game host inspection and loader/unloader operations as
        a cohesive save-game runtime service without moving workflow policy out
        of the command owner.
  - [x] Keep overlay transaction behavior behind its existing class-like
        transaction boundary and remove any redundant loose wrappers.
- [x] Instantiate stateful services at the composition root with their
      run-specific dependencies and inject cohesive instances into command
      owners.
  - [x] Do not inject loose `normalize`, `preflight`, `execute`, `verify`,
        `restore`, resolver, dispatcher, observer, or accessor functions in ad
        hoc dependency tables.
  - [x] Do not introduce globals, service locators, hidden singleton state, or
        imports of the assembled `ds` facade or host internals from command or
        driver service modules.
- [x] Preserve command ownership boundaries.
  - [x] Command modules continue to own normalization, lifecycle orchestration,
        verification policy, receipts, claims, cleanup policy, workflow steps,
        and the public binding contract. Phase 16A supersedes the repeated
        registration and namespace-installation mechanics only.
  - [x] Capability services own reusable runtime interaction only and do not
        construct definitions, register commands, select intrinsic proof, or
        decide cleanup/retry policy.
- [x] Add focused service-contract tests for every new class-like capability.
- [x] Update each representative command suite to prove it consumes cohesive
      capability instances, preserves its existing behavior, and rejects the
      former loose callback-bundle construction shape.
- [x] Add a source-organization check proving representative bindings in
      `ds.lua` pass only class-like stateful services and explicit stateless
