- [x] Representative command modules import only truly stateless helpers and
      receive stateful capabilities only as cohesive service instances.
- [x] `ds.lua` contains composition only, no loose representative framework
      callback bundle remains, and all focused/full/static evidence passes.

Architectural refinement:

- Phase 16A supersedes only the representative registration and public-binding
  mechanics established here. The completed capability-ownership and command-
  policy boundaries remain authoritative: command-specific modules own command
  contracts and cohesive services own runtime interaction. Phase 16A moves the
  repeated `bind(ds, runner, ...)` mechanics into one registrar and requires one
  owning module per command before further family conversion.

